  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 960239,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1988 Carat (Commodore 64) - Synopsis\n\nStep into the political arena with *1988 Carat*, a surprisingly deep and engaging election simulation for the Commodore 64! This 1988 update of the classic *President Elect* puts you in the shoes of a presidential candidate vying for the highest office in the United States. \n\nThe game isn't just about winning; it's about *how* you win. Manage your campaign finances, craft policy positions on crucial issues like the economy, defense, and social welfare, and carefully navigate the media landscape.  You'll need to balance popular appeal with the demands of party loyalists, all while responding to unexpected events and the actions of your opponents. \n\n*1988 Carat* features a dynamic election map, reflecting regional preferences and allowing for targeted campaigning.  Success hinges on shrewd decision-making and a keen understanding of American politics.  Can you secure the nomination, win the general election, and lead the nation?  The fate of the country – and your political career – rests in your hands!"
    },
